# generate-toplists.mjs --dry-run writes full article bodies here for review
scripts/data/runs/

# WordPress migration: one-off tooling + the harvested legacy corpus. Kept out of the branch to
# avoid clutter. NOTE: wp-migration/data holds the only copy of the legacy dates, body text and
# /go/ affiliate targets, which cannot be reconstructed once WordPress is decommissioned — a
# committed snapshot lives at scripts/wp-migration-snapshot.tar.gz, refresh it after any
# re-harvest with:  make -C scripts snapshot   (or see wp-migration/README.md)
scripts/wp-migration/
!scripts/wp-migration-snapshot.tar.gz
